---
title: Salt and Pepper Calamari
description: Crisp, spicy coating and hot, tender squid make an irresistible combination
servings: 4
course: Starter
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 10m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
tags:
- seafood
- starter
- savoury
- chinese
---

= Prepare Calamari =

Cut the @calamari tubes{400%g}(cleaned) tubes in half, from the opening to the tip. Lay them out flat, with the inside facing up, and use a knife to score them diagonally. Cut into 4 cm wide pieces, and chill until needed. 

= Prepare Sides =

Arrange the @iceberg lettuce{8%leaves}(torn), @bean sprouts{150%g}, @spring onion{1}(thinly sliced on diagonal), @cucumber{1}(quartered and cut into thin strips), @fresh coriander{handful}(chopped), @avocado{1%large}(thinly sliced), and @lemon wedges{}, on a serving platter.

= Cook Calamari =

Pat the calamari dry with kitchen paper. Season with the @ground peppercorns{2%tsp}, @sea salt flakes{1.5%tsp}, @chilli flakes{0.5%tsp}, and @Chinese five spice powder{0.5%tsp}, and toss until evenly coated. 

Heat the @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large wok over a very high heat. Cook the calamari in three batches, turning occasionally, for 2 to ~{3%minutes} or until golden.